# Monad testnet on Kuru's own test tokens, hedging on Kuru's books through KuruAdapter.
# Copy to contracts/.env and fill in PRIVATE_KEY (never commit .env). Then, from the repo root:
#
#   npm run deploy:monad-testnet
#   cd backend && NETWORK=monadTestnet node src/index.js        (backend/.env holds the role keys, see below)
#
# Before deploying:
#   - Ask your Kuru integration contact for test tokens (no faucet). A demo needs roughly 300 NVDAx, 100 TSLAx,
#     100 SPYx and 100k USDC, plus MON for gas on every role key.
#   - Kuru's books are thin (about $450 a side per market on Nov 4 2026), so makers quote 1 option at a time
#     on Monad testnet by default (ASK_SIZE / BID_SIZE in backend/.env).
#
# After deploying (addresses are in deployments/monadTestnet.json):
#   - Fund the HedgedMaker with USDC and stock (plain ERC-20 transfers), then from the operator key:
#     hedgedMaker.depositToProtocol(USDC, amount) for the part it quotes against. What stays in the contract is
#     its hedge inventory: USDC to buy stock, stock to sell.
#   - Fund each ShieldedLender with USDC (lender.fund) if you demo Protect.
#   - Fund the maker keys with USDC and stock; makers deposit their whole wallet balance on start.
#
# Check the Kuru side any time (read-only): node backend/scripts/kuru-prices.mjs
# Fork tests: FORK_RPC=https://testnet-rpc.monad.xyz npx hardhat test test/*.fork.test.js   (from contracts/)

PRIVATE_KEY=
MONAD_TESTNET_RPC=https://testnet-rpc.monad.xyz

# Kuru test tokens (decimals: USDC 6, xStocks 18; no multiplier(), so 1:1)
USE_REAL_TOKENS=USDC=0xb01DC575a7ef75e58A05D2bde73ab79f8e7dd0Be,NVDAx=0x1cA0772B36E70ff54525afee1DAEe846Cd914D02,TSLAx=0x7DA7742FCdFD472697A52B0Aaff818CAe3139656,SPYx=0x8BF70Ce58A038f741b4e187ADea126c8cAB867c2

# Kuru venue: deploys KuruAdapter as HedgedMaker's DEX, maps each stock to its market, centres spots and strikes
# on the Kuru mid, and raises the fill-hook gas budget to 1,000,000 (a Kuru hedge is ~430k-490k gas)
KURU_ACCOUNT_CORE=0xe08573a1Ecc4aa507c9626071fA0c4513caf7906
KURU_MARKETS=NVDAx=0xE9C2B9E0F296dbeC9dcc3C8F0F64928F2F8bC081,TSLAx=0x7A53BB8d8A8765418FfE331A02BF5984264922AA,SPYx=0x185Af307dAfd968033337A0180E66B920B4b05Ca
# HOOK_GAS=1000000

# Role addresses (default: the deployer for every role). Use separate keys on anything public.
# MAKER_OPERATOR=0x...
# KEEPER_ADDRESS=0x...
# REPORTER_ADDRESS=0x...
# HEDGER_ADDRESS=0x...
# GUARDIAN_ADDRESS=0x...

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# backend/.env for the same deployment (keys for the roles above; never commit):
#   NETWORK=monadTestnet
#   REPORTER_KEY=0x...     PRICE_SOURCE=kuru is the default when the deployment has a KuruAdapter
#   KEEPER_KEY=0x...
#   OPERATOR_KEY=0x...     runs the HedgedMaker's quotes and hedge ratios
#   MAKER_KEYS=0x...,0x... optional plain maker bots
#   HEDGE_MODE=off         Kuru Flow (the off-chain hedger's venue) has no testnet API; HedgedMaker hedges onchain
#   ASK_SIZE=1             default on Monad testnet
#   BID_SIZE=1
#   RPC_BATCH=1            default on chain 10143: the public testnet RPC rejects JSON-RPC batches
